#
# ThreadSanitizer suppressions, each a proven false positive; TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<this file>.
#
# Boost.Asio's type-erased executor counts its references with a release fetch_sub and an
# acquire std::atomic_thread_fence before the delete (boost/asio/detail/atomic_count.hpp,
# ref_count_down), the correct pattern. TSan does not model atomic_thread_fence, so when two
# copies of one strand are dropped on two threads (a session's socket on the thread stopping
# the node, its aborted read's handler on an io thread) it reports the last one's delete as a
# race with the other's decrement. Reproduced and symbolized on arm64, 2026-11-20
# (HeadsExchange cases pinned to one core); the same frames as CI's unsymbolized report.
race:boost::asio::execution::detail::shared_target_executor::~shared_target_executor
